# DUSA's own music by default: a new save gets Daytona USA '95's The King of
# Speed, Let's Go Away and Sky High on the three DUSA courses, not CCE's
# remixes. National Park Speedway and Desert City keep theirs.
#
# BGM select (Options > Sound): one byte per course at 002FC3A2-002FC3A6,
# an index into the BGM list (patches/bgm_tables.s, docs/music.md): 0-5
# CCE's remixes, Noisy Roars, Pounding Pavement (remix) and the Medley,
# 6-8 the '95 songs, 9-11 CCE's arcade originals, 12 Pounding Pavement '95.
# Until 2026-11-08, 6-8 were CCE's originals (tracks 23-25), taken for
# DUSA's music: a save from then keeps 6-8 and so gets the '95 songs.
# The defaults are a settings block in each overlay that can reset them
# (all load at 06028000): BKUP.BIN 0602B550 copies block + 1 (BGM volume,
# BGM select) and block + 10 into the settings when the backup has no
# save; NAME.BIN and SLCT.BIN carry the same block and routine. Default
# BGM select 0 1 2 3 4 -> 6 7 8 3 4.
DAYTONA/BKUP.BIN 06036F0E 06028000 000102 060708
DAYTONA/NAME.BIN 0603C36A 06028000 000102 060708
DAYTONA/SLCT.BIN 0604182E 06028000 000102 060708

# Options > Sound shows a course's BGM name in yellow when it is the default,
# green otherwise. SLCT.BIN 06031E8C makes that call by comparing the BGM
# index with byte [0603F610 + row], the course-select order map (00 01 02 03
# 04), which only matched the defaults because each course's default was its
# own index. Point it at the default BGM select in the settings block instead
# (the sixth row, the sound test, is always drawn green).
DAYTONA/SLCT.BIN 06031F94 06028000 0603F610 0604182E
